diff --git a/src/hotspot/os/horizon/README.md b/src/hotspot/os/horizon/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..d0b2afbee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/hotspot/os/horizon/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# Horizon HotSpot OS backend
+
+This is an initial static OpenJDK 21 Zero port, not a completed JVM or a Java SE
+compatibility claim. Compilation must be followed by execution of JVM startup,
+class loading, GC, exceptions, threads, native calls and shutdown on hardware.
+
+The existing HotSpot Zero interpreter, safepoints, class machinery and GC stay
+in use. `horizon_bridge.c` isolates libnx's C `Thread`/`Mutex` types from HotSpot's
+C++ classes. The bridge uses documented libnx and Horizon process interfaces.
+
+* Native threads use newlib pthreads with explicit stack sizes and actual libnx
+  stack-mirror bounds. The libnx pthread adapter already assigns workers to
+  all process-permitted cores. It does not implement detached threads, so a
+  native join reaper owns worker tickets and reclaims each finished pthread.
+  The reaper remains alive until process exit; recreating a destroyed JVM is
+  not supported by HotSpot itself.
+* Mutexes, condition variables, events and parkers use the upstream POSIX
+  algorithms adapted to available newlib operations. Relative timeouts use
+  monotonic condition attributes; absolute park deadlines use realtime.
+  `ThreadCritical` recursion is tracked in native TLS before HotSpot TLS exists.
+* A static JNI registry resolves only explicitly registered libraries/symbols.
+  Unregistered ELF libraries fail to load. Native code has process lifetime.
+  Registered tables and names must remain valid until process exit.
+* Memory contracts live separately in `os_horizon_memory.cpp` and the nxvm C
+  backend. The default process heap is shared by malloc, JVM reserves and
+  libraries. Reports never add a Java heap allowance to that process budget.
+* Logical Java paths use the default SD filesystem (`/switch/mineswitch/...`).
+  `getcwd` strips the known `sdmc:` prefix. Path-list separators are `;`, since
+  native libnx device prefixes contain colons.
+* The initial backend requires `-Xrs`, disables PerfData by default and rejects
+  explicitly enabling unsupported signals, PerfData or NUMA. JFR is rejected
+  at compile time until real sampling crash protection exists. Thread CPU time
+  and load averages report unavailable. Process spawning reports `ENOSYS`.
+* Zero uses explicit stack bounds. Recoverable stack guard faults are not
+  advertised. Hardware fault recovery/SafeFetch is a separate bridge concern;
+  checking mappings with `svcQueryMemory` alone does not close an unmap race.
+* The error-report watchdog terminates the process if a report stalls because
+  this backend cannot asynchronously signal a stuck reporting thread.
+
+Default native/JDK paths are `/switch/mineswitch/runtime` and
+`/switch/mineswitch/tmp`; the embedding launcher may set `MINESWITCH_JAVA_HOME`
+before creating the VM. The launcher must create the required directories,
+mount SD storage, initialize socket logging if wanted, register built-in native
+symbols and supply a runtime image built from the same JDK source revision.
